abstract: >-
  GLPlot is a Python plotting library with a Matplotlib-like interface that renders on the GPU
  through OpenGL, so figures with millions of points, dense line families and large 3-D scenes
  stay interactive. It adds GPU density rendering for overplotted data, an interactive
  workstation for editing figures and data live, headless export of images, GIFs and videos
  with style presets, and a Model Context Protocol server through which a language model can
  build, inspect and animate figures.
